Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Configurable goal check intervals

Inspired by Leaf's "configurable goal update interval" (alternative to
Pufferfish's "Throttle goal selector during inactive ticking").

Farm animals (cows, sheep, pigs, chickens, ...) run two relatively
expensive checks while idle:

- TemptGoal scans all players in the world for one holding their food.
- FollowParentGoal (babies only) searches a 17x9x17 box for adults of
  the same type, which gets expensive in crowded breeding pens.

Mobs normally re-run these checks every 2 ticks. This adds
optimizations.goal-check-interval.temptation and .follow-parent to
reef.yml (in ticks, 2 = vanilla) and staggers the checks randomly
between mobs so they don't all run on the same tick.

Changes vanilla behaviour slightly: animals can take up to the
configured interval to notice a player holding food, or to start
following a parent.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/FollowParentGoal.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/FollowParentGoal.java
index 3b158592d97f5ee2ad10b1da75101cb1669871a3..be62f04bf9c0541fda53e18f8f2e8eb563ac15a8 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/FollowParentGoal.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/FollowParentGoal.java
@@ -18,11 +18,26 @@ public class FollowParentGoal extends Goal {
         this.speedModifier = speedModifier;
     }
 
+    private int reefCheckCooldown = -1; // Reef - configurable goal check intervals
+
     @Override
     public boolean canUse() {
         if (this.animal.getAge() >= 0) {
             return false;
         } else {
+            // Reef start - configurable goal check intervals
+            final int checkCalls = dev.reef.ReefConfig.goalCheckCalls(dev.reef.ReefConfig.followParentCheckInterval);
+            if (checkCalls > 1) {
+                if (this.reefCheckCooldown < 0) {
+                    this.reefCheckCooldown = this.animal.getRandom().nextInt(checkCalls); // spread checks out between mobs
+                }
+                if (this.reefCheckCooldown > 0) {
+                    this.reefCheckCooldown--;
+                    return false;
+                }
+                this.reefCheckCooldown = checkCalls - 1;
+            }
+            // Reef end - configurable goal check intervals
             List<? extends Animal> entitiesOfClass = this.animal
                 .level()
                 .getEntitiesOfClass((Class<? extends Animal>)this.animal.getClass(), this.animal.getBoundingBox().inflate(8.0, 4.0, 8.0));
diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/TemptGoal.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/TemptGoal.java
index 18030dc04eb7d7971e457637b5320b1e41665658..3adbef1f8a98c1fe6bf8ea09381d65d0bb178a0e 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/TemptGoal.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/goal/TemptGoal.java
@@ -48,12 +48,27 @@ public class TemptGoal extends Goal {
         this.targetingConditions = TEMPT_TARGETING.copy().selector((entity, level) -> this.shouldFollow(entity));
     }
 
+    private int reefCheckCooldown = -1; // Reef - configurable goal check intervals
+
     @Override
     public boolean canUse() {
         if (this.calmDown > 0) {
             this.calmDown--;
             return false;
         } else {
+            // Reef start - configurable goal check intervals
+            final int checkCalls = dev.reef.ReefConfig.goalCheckCalls(dev.reef.ReefConfig.temptationCheckInterval);
+            if (checkCalls > 1) {
+                if (this.reefCheckCooldown < 0) {
+                    this.reefCheckCooldown = this.mob.getRandom().nextInt(checkCalls); // spread checks out between mobs
+                }
+                if (this.reefCheckCooldown > 0) {
+                    this.reefCheckCooldown--;
+                    return false;
+                }
+                this.reefCheckCooldown = checkCalls - 1;
+            }
+            // Reef end - configurable goal check intervals
             this.player = getServerLevel(this.mob)
                 .getNearestPlayer(this.targetingConditions.range(this.mob.getAttributeValue(Attributes.TEMPT_RANGE)), this.mob);
             // CraftBukkit start
